    "result_text": "Done. The build passes with all tests green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe create audit line is emitted by `AuditOwnerCreated.service(...)` (the final step of `POST /api/owners`). It already logged `id`, `customerCode`, `registrationDate` and `membershipLevel`. I added `membershipNumber`, computed the same way the response DTO derives it \u2014 via `MembershipNumber.of(owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate())` \u2014 so the audited value matches what `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns.\n\nChange in `src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n- Extended the log format with ` membershipNumber={}` and passed the computed number as an argument (existing fields unchanged).\n- Updated the Javadoc to mention the new field.\n\nVerification:\n- New `AcceptanceTest.coreAuditIncludesLevelAndNumber` passes (it asserts the audit line contains both the response's `membershipNumber` and `membershipLevel`).\n- Full `./mvnw test` \u2192 BUILD SUCCESS, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\nThe emitted line now looks like:\n`AUDIT - Owner created: id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E registrationDate=2026-09-08 membershipLevel=2 membershipNumber=NSW-16E6609E-M26`",
